## GNU ld scripts as native library inputs (ImplementationPlan.md 5.10.8,
## 5.10.9 'Sysroot inputs' and 5.9.14; M15.a items 1 and 2; recon p2
## native-imports 2.2 and 7.1). msil-ld reads a script found by -l or given
## on the command line as lld/ELF does (ScriptParser::addFile):
## - GROUP, INPUT and AS_NEEDED name inputs, and -l<name> inside them is
##   searched like -l; OUTPUT_FORMAT and SEARCH_DIR are ignored; comments are
##   comments;
## - an absolute path in a script that lies inside --sysroot is taken under
##   the sysroot (GNU ld's rule; glibc's libc.so names
##   /lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6), and a missing one is lld/ELF's error
##   'cannot find <path> inside <sysroot>';
## - '=<path>' is sysroot-relative;
## - a relative name is looked up in the script's own directory, then in the
##   -L directories; a missing one is lld/ELF's 'unable to find <name>', a
##   missing -l<name> 'unable to find library -l<name>';
## - an input that leads back to a script whose expansion has not ended is
##   the error '<script>:<line>: there is a cycle in linker script inputs'
##   with the two '>>>' lines of 'unable to find <name>', for the input of the
##   script that re-enters, and that input is skipped (the section 12 row of
##   2026-10-23 for 5.10.8 and 5.10.14; lld/ELF's 'there is a cycle in linker
##   script INCLUDEs' is the model): a script naming itself, given on the
##   command line or found by -l, and two scripts naming each other end with
##   exit 1, never a stack overflow. A script read again after its expansion
##   ended (-lc given twice, a script given twice) is no cycle.
## The libraries the script names are bound like any other: libc.so.6,
## libm.so.6, the AS_NEEDED ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 and libmvec.so.1, and
## libc_nonshared.a, whose atexit is native code only. Every file read is
## real: glibc's scripts, shared objects linked by ld.lld from
## Inputs/native/glibc.yaml, and an archive of a native ELF object.

# RUN: rm -rf %t && split-file %s %t && cd %t
# RUN: mkdir -p sys/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu sys/lib64 sys/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu
# RUN: yaml2obj --docnum=1 %S/Inputs/native/glibc.yaml -o libc.o
# RUN: yaml2obj --docnum=2 %S/Inputs/native/glibc.yaml -o libm.o
# RUN: yaml2obj --docnum=3 %S/Inputs/native/glibc.yaml -o ld.o
# RUN: yaml2obj --docnum=4 %S/Inputs/native/glibc.yaml -o mvec.o
# RUN: yaml2obj --docnum=5 %S/Inputs/native/glibc.yaml -o atexit.oS
# RUN: ld.lld -shared -soname libc.so.6 --version-script %S/Inputs/native/glibc-libc.map libc.o \
# RUN:   -o sys/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.so.6
# RUN: ld.lld -shared -soname libm.so.6 --version-script %S/Inputs/native/glibc-libm.map libm.o \
# RUN:   -o sys/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libm.so.6
# RUN: ld.lld -shared -soname ld-linux-x86-64.so.2 --version-script %S/Inputs/native/glibc-ld.map ld.o \
# RUN:   -o sys/lib64/ld-linux-x86-64.so.2
# RUN: ld.lld -shared -soname libmvec.so.1 --version-script %S/Inputs/native/glibc-libmvec.map mvec.o \
# RUN:   -o sys/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libmvec.so.1
# RUN: llvm-ar rcs sys/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc_nonshared.a atexit.oS
# RUN: cp libc.so.txt sys/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libc.so
# RUN: cp libm.so.txt sys/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu/libm.so
# RUN: llvm-as main.ll -o main.o
# RUN: llvm-as atexit.ll -o atexit.o

# DEFINE: %{il} = FileCheck %s --implicit-check-not='"libc"' --implicit-check-not='"libc.so"' \
# DEFINE:   --implicit-check-not='"libm.so"' --implicit-check-not="public hidebysig static pinvokeimpl"
# DEFINE: %{err} = FileCheck %s --implicit-check-not="PLEASE submit" --implicit-check-not="Stack dump" \
# DEFINE:   --implicit-check-not="LLVM ERROR"

## The driver's line for glibc: -L=<dir> under --sysroot, -lc -lm.
# RUN: msil-ld --lto-emit-asm --lto-O0 --sysroot=sys -L=/usr/lib/x86_64-linux-gnu main.o -lc -lm \
# RUN:   -o glibc.il 2>&1 | count 0
# RUN: %{il} --check-prefix=GLIBC --input-file=glibc.il
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=IL-NONE --input-file=glibc.il
# GLIBC-DAG: {{^}}.method assembly hidebysig static pinvokeimpl("libc.so.6" nomangle cdecl) int32 'puts'(native int) cil managed preservesig {}{{$}}
# GLIBC-DAG: {{^}}.method assembly hidebysig static pinvokeimpl("libm.so.6" nomangle cdecl) float64 'cbrt'(float64) cil managed preservesig {}{{$}}
# GLIBC-DAG: {{^}}.method assembly hidebysig static pinvokeimpl("ld-linux-x86-64.so.2" nomangle cdecl) native int '__tls_get_addr'(native int) cil managed preservesig {}{{$}}
# GLIBC-DAG: {{^}}.method assembly hidebysig static pinvokeimpl("libmvec.so.1" nomangle cdecl) float64 '_ZGVbN2v_sin'(float64) cil managed preservesig {}{{$}}
## The %{il} patterns nowhere in the file: for a prefix made only of -DAG
## lines, --implicit-check-not checks only the text before the first match.
# IL-NONE-NOT: "libc"
# IL-NONE-NOT: "libc.so"
# IL-NONE-NOT: "libm.so"
# IL-NONE-NOT: public hidebysig static pinvokeimpl

## The same scripts given on the command line.
